{"parentUuid":"a2e1cda8-2605-4124-ae42-fa8864fc018e","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"insight-01","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"main","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011nKwW9x6HhgYhEvAPxEN8q","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That explains it. On Sep 20 the kernel OOM-killed the export (about 512 MB resident) because the service has MemoryMax=512M and --with-attachments buffers attachments in memory. A SIGKILL skips the shell's EXIT trap, so var/export.pid was left behind. Since then every run finds the file and exits 75 without asking whether the process is alive.\n\nTwo possible fixes: make the wrapper treat a pid file whose process is dead as stale, or stop the export from exceeding the memory limit. The second is ops' call."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":508,"output_tokens":261}},"uuid":"c97ccad8-0c35-412e-a1c5-c11d88d1d10b","timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:33:05.000Z","requestId":"req_011C6DCAzsY7aF8O1gGKkHzd"}
